35,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The neighbouring block’s charge left three households in arrears, and two stopped coming to meetings. That’s a social disaster.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"@Misaki, that’s worrying. But I saw eleven bikes leave between seven and nine, and four times someone had to shift another. It’s a bottleneck.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,May,,"@Shizue, the bottleneck is real. But the ward park costs 2,600 yen a month, and our ledger shows we have no capital for new racks.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,George,,"@May, the ledger is thin. But the treasurer spends three hours a month just reconciling cash. Adding per-place billing would double that.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Mio,,"@George, three hours is a lot. But the minutes show the same flats held the covered spots for five years. No review was ever done.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Mio, five years without review? That explains the resentment. But if we charge, we risk the same social collapse as the neighbours.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Misaki, I agree. The rain exposure is bad too. Saddles are wet every morning past the downpipe. We need a fairer physical setup.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,"@Shizue, fair is good, but if we can’t afford it, it’s a dream. The ward park is full, so we can’t just send people there.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,George,,"@May, the supplier’s frame took twenty seconds to load and needs greasing twice a year. That’s a maintenance trap.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@George, maintenance is a worry. But the sticker register shows daily riders would rather pay than be counted as equal. They want priority.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Mio, if they want to pay, that’s a signal. But the complaint log had nine notes about leaning bikes, and none were resolved.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Misaki, unresolved complaints breed resentment. I want a system where the morning isn’t a shoving match.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,May,,"@Shizue, I understand. But we need a source of income. If we don’t charge, who pays for the new racks?","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,George,,"@May, if we charge, I’m the one doing the bookkeeping. I can’t do three hours a month plus the new billing.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@George, that’s a valid point. But if we don’t fix the bias, the grumbling will never stop.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Misaki,,I’m leaning towards a system that doesn’t rely on constant enforcement. The complaint log shows we have no one to ask.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shizue,,I agree. I want the morning to be calm. I’ll support whatever reduces the shoving.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,May,,I need to see the options. I can’t decide without knowing the financial impact.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,George,,I need to see the options. I can’t take on more work without knowing the scope.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Mio,,I need to see the options. I want to end the bias.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
