60,3,1,talk,Misaki,,Option A charges monthly. That’s what broke the neighbours. I worry it will isolate people here too.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Option B is open racks. No one owns a spot. That might stop the shoving, but will it stop the rain?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,May,,"Option A brings in money. That’s the only way we can afford new racks. I’m worried about the social cost, but the budget is empty.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,George,,"Option A means I do the billing. I can’t do that. Option B means no billing, but who maintains the racks?","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Mio,,"Option C is a lottery. It’s fair on paper. But if the same people win every year, the bias continues.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Mio, a lottery is random, but it’s not dynamic. If someone moves, the spot stays. That’s rigid.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Misaki, rigidity is bad. But Option B’s open racks mean anyone can use any spot. That’s flexible.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,May,,"@Shizue, flexibility is good, but it’s free. Who pays for the racks? Option A pays for them.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,George,,"@May, Option A pays for them, but I pay with my time. I can’t do the bookkeeping.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Mio,,"@George, I hear you. But Option C is the fairest. It gives everyone a chance.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Mio, fairness is good, but if it doesn’t solve the morning chaos, it’s useless. Option B solves the chaos.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Misaki, I agree. Option B solves the chaos. I’m voting B.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,May,,"@Shizue, I understand. But I can’t ignore the budget. I’m voting A to fund the racks.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,George,,"@May, I can’t do the work for A. I’m voting B to avoid the billing.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Mio,,"@George, I agree. Option C is fair, but Option B is practical. I’m voting B.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Misaki,,I’m voting B. It avoids the social collapse of A and the rigidity of C.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Shizue,,I’m voting B. It makes the morning calm.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,May,,I’m voting A. We need the money.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,George,,I’m voting B. I can’t do the work.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Mio,,I’m voting B. It’s practical.,"{""words"":5,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
